# wiki+ prototype — Caddy reverse proxy + automatic TLS (issue A.2 / #42).
#
# Caddy terminates TLS directly (Let's Encrypt, HTTP-01 by default) and reverse-proxies to
# the app container over the compose network. Cloudflare EDGE CACHE is deferred to the
# production-MVP (issue #35) — for the prototype Caddy is the public-facing TLS endpoint.
#
# The canonical public host is `wikiplus.video`. It resolves DNS-ONLY (a plain A/AAAA record
# straight to the box IP — no Cloudflare proxy in front), so Caddy reaches Let's Encrypt
# directly and the HTTP-01 challenge just works. Keep the record DNS-only: putting a proxy in
# front means Caddy's ACME challenge must contend with the edge intercepting :80/:443 and the
# proxy's SSL/TLS mode has to be "Full"/"Full (strict)" or the origin loops — avoided entirely
# by pointing DNS at the box.
#
# `wikiplus.wikiedu.org` (the former host, a subdomain of the wikiedu.org zone) is kept ONLY as
# a permanent redirect to the canonical host so existing links, bookmarks, and indexed URLs
# keep resolving. Caddy still obtains a cert for it to serve the HTTPS redirect.
{
	# Operator contact for Let's Encrypt / ACME (expiry + policy notices).
	email sage@wikiedu.org
}

wikiplus.video {
	# Reverse-proxy to the app container (compose service name : container port).
	reverse_proxy app:3000

	encode zstd gzip

	# Access logs to stdout (captured by `docker compose logs caddy`), JSON for easy parsing.
	log {
		output stdout
		format json
	}
}

# Former host → canonical host. 301 permanent, preserving the full path + query ({uri}).
wikiplus.wikiedu.org {
	redir https://wikiplus.video{uri} permanent
}
